1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,935
Captain Marcus Webb was alone on the bridge
when the mine-clearance report came in.

2
00:00:06,975 --> 00:00:12,563
One of the narrowest throats on earth,
carrying a fifth of the world's oil,

3
00:00:12,603 --> 00:00:15,415
was opening again after six days shut.

4
00:00:15,455 --> 00:00:21,590
Sarah Callahan came up without her camera
— for the first time since the war began.

5
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:23,822
“The strait's open,” she said.

6
00:00:23,862 --> 00:00:25,235
“Limited,” he said.

7
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:26,798
“Northern lane only.”

8
00:00:26,838 --> 00:00:28,360
“Still open, though.”

9
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,368
He nodded without speaking.

10
00:00:30,408 --> 00:00:34,237
On the horizon, the silhouette
of a tanker appeared.

11
00:00:34,277 --> 00:00:36,692
“I heard about Fordow,” she said.

12
00:00:36,732 --> 00:00:39,593
“It's not over, is it.” “Probably not.”

13
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:44,578
He knew that the strait opening
today didn't mean the war was over.

14
00:00:44,618 --> 00:00:47,742
Not while Fordow's signal was still alive.
